<BaseLayout title="About US Travel Guide" description="US Travel Guide brings practical travel decisions together, with transparent official sources and clear limits on what we have verified." path="/about/"><section class="container section-block"><div class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A useful starting point</p><h1>Make the small decisions<br/>with more confidence.</h1></div><div class="prose"><p>US Travel Guide is an independent travel-planning resource. We focus on questions that sit between an inspiring photograph and a workable day out: how to reach a place, which ticket covers a journey, what to compare, and where to confirm a changing detail.</p><h2>What you will find here</h2><p>Our guides combine official references with practical explanations and comparisons. They are written to help you understand your options, rather than to replace the transport operator, attraction or public agency responsible for a service.</p><h2>What a source check means</h2><p>A source-check date tells you when the cited information was reviewed. It is not a guarantee that a price, timetable or operating rule will remain unchanged. Time-sensitive details link to the responsible organization.</p><h2>Our editorial approach</h2><p>We distinguish research from firsthand experience. We do not invent visits, personal recommendations or author credentials. Read our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> for how we use automated tools, handle sources and review corrections.</p><h2>Independence and support</h2><p>Any future advertising will be identified and kept separate from editorial decisions. See our <a href="/advertising/">advertising disclosure</a> and <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
